Build Dawn for HarmonyOS, so WebGPU has a decoder to run on.

use_dawn left OHOS out, so the GPU process had no WebGPU decoder and every
WebGPU context failed ("Failed to create WebGPU Context Provider") even with
--enable-unsafe-webgpu. Dawn's Vulkan backend then needs the loader by the
name HarmonyOS gives it, libvulkan.so, as on Android; OHOS is otherwise
taken for Linux there, which looks for libvulkan.so.1.

An experiment: sharing images between Dawn and the compositor, which a
WebGPU canvas needs, is not wired up on OHOS.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 (Dawn 8597a1aaec54).

diff --git a/third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/vulkan/BackendVk.cpp b/third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/vulkan/BackendVk.cpp
index a93ea4f..2c38742 100644
--- a/third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/vulkan/BackendVk.cpp
+++ b/third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/vulkan/BackendVk.cpp
@@ -58,7 +58,9 @@ constexpr char kSwiftshaderLibName[] = "libvk_swiftshader.dylib";
 #endif
 
 #if DAWN_PLATFORM_IS(LINUX)
-#if DAWN_PLATFORM_IS(ANDROID)
+#if DAWN_PLATFORM_IS(ANDROID) || defined(__OHOS__)
+// HarmonyOS, like Android, ships its loader as libvulkan.so with no
+// versioned name.
 constexpr char kVulkanLibName[] = "libvulkan.so";
 #else
 constexpr char kVulkanLibName[] = "libvulkan.so.1";
